//
// Expected: a0 at one session, a1 at two.
//
// Alice's tag = MAC(k, x) is the same in every session. At two sessions the
// attacker replaces x at Alice with nil, so Alice sends MAC(k, nil) and Bob's
// check would halt him; the attacker delivers the tag Alice#2 sends in its
// place. Bob and Bob#2 both pass their checks on MAC(k, x), which Alice sent
// once: duplicate acceptance. auth_withheld_static_replay.vp halts the sender
// instead of diverting it. The search once only filled receives whose sender
// never sent, and never restored the honest input at a recipient that the
// tampered sender made halt. At one session no other Alice sends MAC(k, x):
// a0. Leaving Alice unstarted gives the same attack, so
// auth_tampered_static_replay_guarded.vp, which cannot divert Alice, reaches
// the same verdicts.
attacker[active]

principal Carol[
	knows private x
]

Carol -> Alice: x

principal Alice[
	knows private k
	tag = MAC(k, x)
]

Alice -> Bob: tag

principal Bob[
	knows private k
	knows private x
	_ = ASSERT(tag, MAC(k, x))?
]

queries[
	authentication? Alice -> Bob: tag
]
